Task 4: Classification with Logistic Regression. 

Project Goal:
To implement and thoroughly evaluate foundational classification models (Logistic Regression) for a Breast Cancer Winsconsin Dataset.

Key Outcomes & Skills:
a. Classifier Development: Implemented a Logistic Regression model for a binary classification task (e.g., medical diagnosis), demonstrating understanding of how the model transforms linear output into probability via the Sigmoid Function.
b. Deep Evaluation: Utilized the Confusion Matrix to break down classification results, and critically evaluated the model using Precision, Recall, and F1-Score.
c. Performance Visualization: Generated the ROC (Receiver Operating Characteristic) Curve and calculated the AUC (Area Under the Curve) score to assess the model's discriminative power across all thresholds.
d. Threshold Management: Demonstrated the ability to select or tune the classification threshold based on the specific business need (e.g., prioritizing Recall to minimize False Negatives).


Technical Stack:
Category: Tool / Concept
Libraries: Scikit-learn (LogisticRegression)
Concepts: Binary Classification, Sigmoid Function, Confusion Matrix, Precision/Recall, ROC-AUC, Threshold Tuning
Dataset Used: Breast Cancer Wisconsin Dataset 
